# Configuration
#
# `.env` IS committed on purpose: Flutter can only read files that are listed
# as assets (see pubspec.yaml), and a fresh clone must build without a manual
# copy step. It therefore contains only non-secret development defaults.
#
# Real secrets never belong here - they live in git-ignored native files:
#   android/app/src/main/res/values/strings.xml   (Facebook App ID / token)
#   android/app/google-services.json              (Firebase)
#   ios/Runner/GoogleService-Info.plist           (Firebase)
# or are injected at build time with --dart-define (see .env.example).
.env.local
.env.*.local
!.env.example

# Firebase config
android/app/google-services.json
ios/Runner/GoogleService-Info.plist

# Signing
android/key.properties
*.jks
*.keystore

# Apple certs
*.p12
*.cer
*.pem
*.cer
# Facebook config
#
# android/app/src/main/res/values/strings.xml is deliberately NOT ignored.
# Facebook's App ID and Client Token are public-by-design (they ship inside
# every app binary), and AndroidManifest.xml hard-references them - so a
# fresh clone must contain them or the build breaks.